## Council follow-up

Council requested an explicit content-use signal in every robots group, absolute canonical header URLs, and article-only breadcrumb scope. The robots test first failed against the missing named-group directive before the production fix. The deployment property now rejects a relative canonical header. Breadcrumb eligibility explicitly matches only `/lore/` and `/systems/`, with a generated-path property covering other collections and the homepage. The fence-link explanation above now cites the real backlink renderer rather than a route constant.

The follow-up passed `pnpm turbo run check test build --concurrency=1`: 91 of 91 tasks, including 732 site tests, 95 reader tests and 92 deployment tests. A breadcrumb mutation admitting `/skills/` failed the new eligibility property before restoration. Static startup is now 1,095,669 bytes for Mischief, 130 bytes above the initial patch and 407 bytes above the prepared baseline. Other workers and all ceilings remain unchanged. The added runtime bytes implement the council-requested absolute headers and repeated policy directive; page data stays static.

## Verification before initial commit

- `pnpm turbo run check test build`: passed, 91 of 91 tasks; site suite 90 files and 730 tests. This was the completed working-tree gate before commit, not a deployment check.
- Property mutation: removing JSON-LD `<` escaping made the reader metadata test fail. The safe serializer was restored.
- Route mutation: removing the sitemap's workshop-child filter made the live-handler seam fail on `/tokenmaxx/exercises`. The filter was restored.
- Deployment-check mutation: ignoring the Markdown canonical header made the property fail with an unexpected pass verdict. Header validation was restored. Each new deployment verdict is checked independently, so unrelated failures cannot mask a missing guard.
- Built reader HTML contains `WebSite` with `SoftwareSourceCode` on `/`, and `TechArticle` plus `BreadcrumbList` on `/lore/init-runs-twice`.
- The generated manifest contains no route for this queue and no `/data/` page. The queue stays an audit artifact.
- The Brain prose checker passes. The artifact uses `.svx` rather than the originally requested `.md`, per the brief amendment on 2026-11-08. No checker or baseline was changed.

Static startup bytes, measured with `apps/site/scripts/startup-budget.ts` after preparing the original build and again through the changed gate:

| Worker | Before | After | Ceiling |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| Mischief | 1,095,262 | 1,095,539 | 1,114,000 |
| LearnFeedbackAuth | 1,515,207 | 1,515,207 | 1,516,000 |
| Workshop | 731,416 | 731,416 | 870,000 |
| TurboCache | 475,734 | 475,734 | 480,000 |

Mischief grew by 277 bytes for runtime policy and link output. The growing page metadata remains static build output. No ceiling or dependency pin changed. The auth worker's existing headroom remains narrow at 793 bytes.

## Maintenance candidates and missing evidence

- Reduce `/log` HTML weight without hiding useful history behind client-only rendering. Baseline: 1,600,407 bytes of HTML. The page implementation was outside this packet.
- Review the four duplicate title pairs against distinct user intent. Do not merge based on the title alone.
- Check IndexNow setup. No key file or submission integration was found in repository search. No submission was made. Add a verified key and submit only changed canonical URLs if the owner chooses to enable it; acknowledgement does not mean indexed.
- Use the supplied Search Console page/query aggregates as a baseline, but obtain URL inspection and Google-selected canonical data before claiming index coverage or canonical adoption. Impressions do not prove the current indexed state of every URL.
- Obtain Bing Webmaster data and inspect individual backlinks before classifying link quality, loss or spam. The OpenSEO overview supplies domain totals only.
- Keep person pages focused on public work. Their larger impression counts do not justify targeting personal attributes, appearance or demographic queries.
- Run a real answer-engine panel with web retrieval and retained response/citation evidence. The six search queries are a baseline proxy only.
- Measure mobile Core Web Vitals through CrUX or PageSpeed, or record a clearly labeled Lighthouse lab run. Current response timings do not substitute.
- After deployment, repeat the sitemap crawl, inspect raw HTML JSON-LD and response headers, and verify that no sitemap URL returns `noindex`. Before deployment, local passing tests do not establish changed live behavior.
